    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`python/pyproject_xpu.toml` pins `sglang-kernel-xpu` to the `v0.2.0+xpu` release wheel in `sgl-project/whl`. Kernel changes merged to `sgl-kernel-xpu` main are not picked up until a new release wheel is built and published via `release-whl-kernel-xpu.yml` and this URL is bumped.\n\n## Modifications\n\nPoint the dependency at the `sgl-kernel-xpu` main branch instead of the release wheel:\n\n```diff\n-  \"sglang-kernel-xpu @ https://github.com/sgl-project/whl/releases/download/v0.2.0+xpu/sglang_kernel_xpu-0.2.0-cp310-abi3-manylinux_2_38_x86_64.whl\",\n+  \"sglang-kernel-xpu @ git+https://github.com/sgl-project/sgl-kernel-xpu.git@main\",\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- With a git reference, `pip install .` builds `sglang-kernel-xpu` from source (scikit-build-core + CMake). The install environment needs the oneAPI/SYCL toolchain (`source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh`), and install time increases.\n- Installs are no longer reproducible across time since `main` moves.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] `stage-a-test-1-gpu-xpu` passes on this PR (verifies the source build works in the XPU CI image)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #38114119346](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38114119346)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38114119293](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38114119293)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38114119385](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38114119385)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n\nSupersedes #41085 (moved the branch into sgl-project/sglang so it can be cloned directly with `-b xpu/kernel-from-main`).\n",
